    "title": "Man in custody after gun goes off on SEPTA 13th Street trolley platform - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By John McDevitt ,\n4 hours ago Mike DeNardo/KYW Newsradio (file) PHILADELPHIA (KYW Newsradio) — A man is in custody after SEPTA police said his gun discharged on a Center City trolley platform on Wednesday.\nAccording to SEPTA, the incident happened around 2 p.m. it was around 2 o'clock. A man on the 13th Street platform was fidgeting with a gun in his waistband when authorities said the weapon went off.\nOfficials said the man fled and hopped on a westbound trolley. He was stopped at the 40th Street station by SEPTA transit police and taken into custody.\nA woman was injured, possibly by shrapnel. She was taken to a hospital for observation. An investigation is underway.",
    "summary": "55 minutes ago Mike DeNardo/KYW Newsradio (file) PHILADELPHIA (KYW Newsradio) — A man is in custody after SEPTA police said his gun discharged on a Center City trolley platform on Wednesday. According to SEPTA, the incident happened around 2 p.m. it was around 2 o'clock. A man on the 13th Street platform was fidgeting with a gun in his waistband when authorities said the weapon went off. Officials said the man fled and hopped on a westbound trolley. He was stopped at the 40th Street station by SEPTA transit police and taken into custody.",
